# AI STUDENT MENTOR — PROJECT RULES

1. This is an existing project. Never recreate it from scratch.
2. Preserve the existing Flask backend, JSON datasets, integrations and tests.
3. Frontend technology is HTML, CSS, Vanilla JavaScript and Chart.js.
4. Backend technology is Python Flask.
5. Never introduce React, Vue, Angular, Node.js, Express, MongoDB or MySQL.
6. No production database or paid API dependency.
7. Use existing API utilities and local JSON demo fallbacks.
8. Never expose API secrets in frontend code.
9. Clearly label demo data and sample jobs.
10. Do not claim demo scores are actual ML predictions.
11. Maintain Windows 11 and PowerShell compatibility.
12. Do not remove or weaken existing tests.
13. Run pytest -v after meaningful changes.
14. Prefer small, maintainable and reusable modules.
15. Do not overwrite .env, .venv or user configuration.
16. Inspect existing code before editing.
17. Explain files created and modified.
18. Do not claim functionality was tested unless it was actually tested.
19. Work sequentially through the project's development batches.
20. Preserve working functionality while adding features.